WEBVTT

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.280
Ieyasu was this powerful?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.840
I was the one who was meant 
to activate the armor.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.190
Date Masamune, just who are you?

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.300
How do you know so much about this?

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:36.470
From your perspective, 
we're from the distant future.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.760
The future?

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.990
Yes.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.710
But to be more specific,

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:45.580
we're from the far future of the 
space-time continuum's temporal axis.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.730
But under the multiple worlds interpretation,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.360
we've traversed the event plane

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.300
via localized fluctuation of the 
entropic phase-system that results

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.520
So you're from another country, yeah?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.520
in the most proximate value of the wave function,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.080
when solved for the differentiated limit 
of a seventh-order equation,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.600
That's about right.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.300
of a saturated membrane universe structure...

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.970
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.970
<b>Battle Maiden</b>

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:48.820
My lord!

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.560
Congratulations on attaining your cherished desire.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.270
Congratulations.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.150
Please issue your first order as ruler.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.770
Then disappear.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.280
Did you not hear me?

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.100
Disappear.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.120
My lord?

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.090
I'm not interested in useless losers.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.040
Get lost.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.300
Out of the way!

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.160
She destroyed the barrier with one blast.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.490
Wow!

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:31.320
Let's go!

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.020
Yes!

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.320
Wake up!

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.250
What happened up there?

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.820
Tokugawa's shinobi?

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:51.750
Answer me!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.780
What is Ieyasu doing up there?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.420
She has put on the Crimson Armor...

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.840
But she herself has changed.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.900
The Tokugawa clan have been

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.430
masters of the dark arts for years.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.850
And our lord, in particular, inherited this talent.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:17.140
But I never thought that this would happen.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:18.860
How horrible.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.610
Please show us mercy!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.110
Please... Please save her!

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.120
My lord...

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.100
Never.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.710
This was all her own doing.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.410
You're so full.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.590
You want to do some damage, too, right?

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.220
All right... I'll release you now.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:00.230
My lord!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.010
Wonderful... You really let loose, didn't you?

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.020
Ieyasu...

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.130
All forces, withdraw!

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:37.980
My lord...

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.120
You wouldn't stand a chance if you got hit

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.550
by one of those blasts.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.190
For now, withdraw.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.600
No, my lord!

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.010
As Owari warriors, we cannot retreat,

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.490
leaving you behind!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.990
Order us to be your shield and die for you.

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:57.250
Did you think I wanted you to simply run?

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.590
You are to split up

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:04.760
and evacuate the people in the castle town.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.030
If you are warriors of Owari,

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.760
then shield its people, not its lord.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:11.800
Yes, my lord!

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.900
Why are you still here?

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:21.990
You told me that you and I are one.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.820
I cannot run away.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:29.020
I can't leave you or Tokunyan!

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.320
I have nowhere else to go, anyway.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.610
You two are beyond help.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.080
And Masamune...

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.450
What of you?

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:41.850
I wish to see, to the end, the fate of those

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.540
who wear the Crimson Armor.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:48.050
And I am her guardian.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.050
Sensei...

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.850
As you like.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.050
Nobunaga-dono,

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.370
what is this?

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.310
Yoshimoto-dono, what are you doing here?

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.460
That is the seal of the Tokugawa clan...

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.310
Just what is happening up there?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.940
Tokunyan stole my lord's armor!

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.320
And then she started going on a rampage...

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.620
Ieyasu-chan, it's dangerous to stand there!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.950
Come down from there!

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.800
Ieyasu-chan!

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.740
Can you hear me?

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.750
That stupid old bag...

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.960
She's never shown me any respect!

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.540
You fool!

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:32.630
My lord!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:34.640
My lord!

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:43.900
I'm glad...

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:45.940
Nobunaga-dono.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.760
You understand now, right?

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.400
That's how she really is.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.650
Ieyasu-chan...

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.350
How wonderful.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.850
The lightning is getting stronger.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:25.650
What are you going to do?

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:33.030
My lord, please forgive me.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.530
Wait, Mitsuhide!

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.170
Mitsuhide!

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.420
<i>My life is for my lord!</i>

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:51.130
Akechi Mitsuhide is here!

00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:59.430
Ieyasu, prepare to die!

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:08.560
Hey, the idiot with the glasses wants to touch me.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:11.900
Mitsuhide!

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.740
Akerin!

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.370
Akerin!

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.370
Nobunaga-dono.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.600
Is this all we can expect of 
the Sixth Heaven's Demon King?

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.590
Thank you.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.380
I'm in your debt.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.160
My lord...

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.820
I'm sorry!

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.910
I shamed you with that pathetic attack.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.080
Fool.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:52.940
Never do that again!

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.700
Are you trying to take years off my life?

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.330
What's going on up there?

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:33.870
I see...

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.730
This is indeed a dark hour.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:41.350
Were you gathering the Crimson Armor, 
even cognizant of its dangers?

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.680
Had the armor not been gathered,

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.780
Ieyasu-chan would never have become like that.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.130
You've paid a high price 
for your attempt at conquest.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.220
Everyone...

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.630
I beg you, everyone.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.130
I beg you...

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:04.910
For now, we must stop Ieyasu, so she cannot

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.150
harm the innocent peasants.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:10.730
Afterwards, I shall gladly take any blame.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.150
But right now, please help me!

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.650
My lord...

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:23.090
Jeez... I can't say no to that.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:26.980
I blame the armor, not Ieyasu-chan.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:29.650
They will speak for generations of the day

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:31.830
when Oda Nobunaga bowed her head.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.260
You guys...

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.670
You all look like you're having fun.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.550
Don't think you can leave us out.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:45.600
You?

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.100
The star of the show always arrives late.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.000
Never seen them before.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:50.850
Who are they?

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.620
If you don't know, then I shall—

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:58.420
This is Mouri Motonari, Chousokabe Motochika,

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:00.110
and Ootomo Sourin.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.610
What has brought you to Owari?

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.560
Something has been bothering us.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:12.120
You had a premonition of the disaster 
the armor would bring.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:14.120
The same that we had.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:18.880
So that's the cause?

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:22.780
Dodge it!

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.240
Wh-What?

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:30.620
What is that?

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.490
Ieyasu's lightning.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:33.840
Good timing.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.170
Help us.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.610
We're going to defeat her.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.690
Then that was all just talk?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.200
That isn't true.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:47.640
My lord, what will happen to Tokunyan,

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.390
after we defeat the Crimson Armor?

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.200
She won't escape unscathed.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.330
Then Tokunyan...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.250
Don't say another word, Hideyoshi.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.880
Ieyasu is a warrior.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.430
If she planned on conquering the land,

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.660
then she was prepared for this.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:06.760
But...

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:10.210
If she dies in this battle, that was the destiny

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.770
heaven had ordained for her.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:16.270
But... But are you OK with that, Yoshimoto-san?

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:20.890
I'm not!

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.490
Everyone, don't kill Tokunyan!

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:30.780
No...

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.830
You tell us not to kill her?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.330
It will be far more difficult 
to let her live than to kill her.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:42.840
You always ask the impossible.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.000
My lord?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.250
Believe in me.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:52.720
What do you think?

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.540
It will be difficult.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.730
But some things are worth doing 
because they're difficult.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:01.980
That's what war is!

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:04.900
Everyone...

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.490
I'll tell you again, Hideyoshi.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:08.740
Believe in me.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.490
Believe in my lord...

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:14.270
Let us go, then!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.210
Nobunaga's changed...

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:30.400
Ieyasu!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.430
Lots of easy targets.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.280
We can't even get close?

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.180
Curse you, Ieyasu!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:02.540
My lord, she's too strong 
for us to attack separately.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:05.550
Then what do we do?

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.300
You seem to have a plan.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:15.310
Numbers don't make weaklings any stronger.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:22.440
<i>Suzaku Adamantine Crasher!</i>

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:26.190
<i>Flame Dragon Fan Strike!</i>

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.120
I guess that's your only trick.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.150
Go!

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:47.070
<i>Don Frankie Cannon!</i>

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.480
Stupid little cannon...

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.010
Ieyasu-chan!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.610
Old bag!

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:04.970
"Old bag"?

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:06.860
Old bag! Old bag! Old bag! Old bag!

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:08.690
Enough, already.

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:11.280
<i>Gale Void Wave!</i>

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.950
<i>Mountain Slasher!</i>

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.180
<i>Lightning Spear Flurry!</i>

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:37.760
You wimps never give up.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.770
Then how does it feel to be defeated by wimps?

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:49.150
<i>Dance of the Black Funeral!</i>

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:25.020
Nobunaga...

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:27.020
Here I go!

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:32.320
<i>Cruel Blade!</i>

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.530
<i>Shining Demon Cir—</i>

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:00.800
My lord!

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:38.300
Enough of this, Ieyasu!

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:01.860
My lord...

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:03.430
Everyone...

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.500
You awake?

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:27.960
What happened...

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.100
You had a bad dream.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.730
My lord...

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:35.600
You guys. You survived?

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:37.230
We're so glad you're safe...

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:41.810
You're useless, but you sure are hard to kill.

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:43.690
Yes. Thank you...

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:44.870
Thank you!

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:45.990
That's not a compliment!

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.980
I guess they match their lord,

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.500
and she matches them.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:55.930
My lord...

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:58.410
Well done, Mitsuhide.

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:01.320
Without your plan, we couldn't have won.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:03.470
But the castle...

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.510
We can build another castle.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.790
What matters are the people.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:09.520
Right?

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:10.980
Right!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.540
Ieyasu...

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.770
Anything to say to us?

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.420
Your voice is too soft.

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:23.280
We can't hear you.

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.290
Louder!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.070
I-I'm very sorry!

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:35.120
Sorry!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.840
I was wrong!

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.840
You should've just said that at the start.

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:42.840
Y-Yes.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.510
People should be honest about what they feel.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:46.850
Right, Mitsuhide?

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:47.570
Yes.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.640
Nobunaga-sama, I have a request.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:54.760
From now on, allow me to 
call you Nobunaga-oneesama.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:55.470
What?

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:56.860
N-Neesama...

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:01.450
Nobunaga-oneesama, please let me stay

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:04.360
by your side, to atone for what I've done.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:10.450
Your elegance and beauty has convinced me...

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.460
You're the person I'm fated for!

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.040
What?!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.030
My lord is mine!

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.210
Remove your hand, you glasses-wearing idiot.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:26.470
W-Wait, Ieyasu-chan... 
What are you talking about?

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.480
No!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.350
Stop!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:38.480
Save me, Nobunaga-oneesama!

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:43.520
Nobunaga-oneesama!

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:45.980
Don't say that!

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:48.490
Everyone's back to normal!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.920
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.920
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:52.450
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:29.420
Sometimes I worry,

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:34.970
I feel like giving up, or I run into problems.

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:52.450
<b>Thinking</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.720
But a day has twenty-four hours, 
and time never stops.

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:45.440
So I try to spend as little time as I can 
being sad or down.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:49.440
And no matter what happens, I try to have fun,

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:52.450
with a smile on my face.

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.330
Make sure you watch next time!

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.960
Preview

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.960
Sunlight Maiden
